7,"Löyöp language : Name, Phonology, Grammar, Bibliography Wikipedia, the ...",http://fr.edu.vn/en/Löyöp_language,"The name Löyöp[løjøp] used since 2009 [4][5][6] refers to the area called ""Divers' Bay"" in English, in the eastern part of Ureparapara. It derives from a Proto-Torres-Banks form * loroβi, with cognates in Lehali Loyēp[lɔjɪp]. The now-deprecated name Lehalurup once used by certain authors (e.g. Tryon) is likely a result from a transcription error, possibly under the influence of ...",Löyöp,Austronesian
8,Indigenous Taiwanese Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/indigenous-taiwanese-music,"Indigenous Taiwanese music encompasses the vocal and instrumental traditions of Taiwan's Austronesian peoples (including Amis, Atayal, Paiwan, Bunun, Puyuma, Rukai, Tsou, Saisiyat, Tao/Yami, Thao, Truku/Seediq, and others).",Löyöp,Austronesian
9,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures. These influences have over the centuries introduced new instruments, styles, and genres, blending age-old elements with newer traditions.",Löyöp,Austronesian
